                            "In English, age and nationality use the verb to be. “I'm 30.” “I'm Mexican.” Say “I'm 30”, never “I have 30”.",
                            "With jobs we say a/an: “I'm a nurse.” “He's an engineer.” Nationality words are adjectives: from Spain → I'm Spanish; from Mexico → I'm Mexican."], examples: [
