                            "Possessive words go before the thing: my, your, his, her. “This is my bag.” “That's your coat.” “Her name is Ana.”",
                            "To ask about the owner: “Is this your …?” or “Whose is this?” The answer repeats the owner: “It's mine.” / “No, it's his.”"], examples: [
